cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GLASS, please cite the paper."
title: "GLASS: A Closed-Form Encoder-Geometric Detector for Machine-Generated Text"
abstract: >-
  GLASS scores a document by the difference between its squared residual to a human
  subspace and the smallest squared residual to a library of per-generator AI
  subspaces, all obtained in closed form by truncated SVD on a frozen sentence
  encoder. It requires no language-model inference and no training at scoring time.
